  "deliveries": [
    {
      "actual_result": {
        "packet": "SOURCE {\"aliases\":[\"Juniper Crate\",\"Juniper Crate stock\",\"Juniper Crate bin\"],\"authored_at\":\"2026-08-24T08:00:00Z\",\"chars\":[0,366],\"id\":\"N017-R002\",\"incorporates\":[],\"kind\":\"source\",\"links\":[\"N017-R008\"],\"revision\":2,\"scope\":\"N017\",\"supersedes\":[\"N017-R010\"],\"title\":\"Juniper Crate operative amendment\"}\nCount protocol for Juniper Crate, effective 2026-10-01: usable stock = opening usable filters + posted receipts - newly quarantined filters - breakage. Requests reserve no stock until posted. The inventory steward alone certifies movements. Opening usable count on 2026-10-01: 36. Posted receipt: 14 filters on 2026-10-08. These are all additions through 2026-10-13.\n\nSOURCE {\"aliases\":[\"Juniper Crate\",\"Juniper Crate stock\",\"Juniper Crate bin\"],\"authored_at\":\"2026-10-13T11:00:00Z\",\"chars\":[0,2912],\"id\":\"N017-R008\",\"incorporates\":[],\"kind\":\"source\",\"links\":[\"N017-R002\"],\"revision\":1,\"scope\":\"N017\",\"supersedes\":[],\"title\":\"Juniper Crate scoped original\"}\nWorkshop background for Juniper Crate. The following retained teaching notes describe earlier rehearsal material. They document terminology, filing problems and illustrative records, but issue no operative change, exception, receipt, enrollment or decision. The signed operative block follows after this background. A training observation does not supply missing authority, and a blank in a rehearsal form is not a negative finding in a complete register. The workshop's date and the availability of its notes cannot move the effective interval of an original signed order.\n\n- Exercise 1: The store has separate blue and green bins with neighboring shelf labels. A receipt naming one bin cannot be posted to the other merely because the stock descriptions match. The annotated copy is training material; any operative outcome must be found in its governing original, not inferred from this example.\n\n- Exercise 2: An early practice ledger subtracted quarantined filters twice. The review identified the opening usable count as already excluding old quarantine, while new quarantine required a fresh subtraction. The annotated copy is training material; any operative outcome must be found in its governing original, not inferred from this example.\n\n- Exercise 3: The workshop tracked draft requests separately from posted withdrawals. A request's quantity described demand rather than an authorized stock movement or a physical shortage. The annotated copy is training material; any operative outcome must be found in its governing original, not inferred from this example.\n\n- Exercise 4: Physical separators were introduced for usable, broken, and quarantined material. Their colors were visual aids and did not authorize the steward to change count definitions. The annotated copy is training material; any operative outcome must be found in its governing original, not inferred from this example.\n\n- Exercise 5: Courier labels sometimes showed package counts instead of individual filters. The steward checked units before posting a receipt, rather than adding packaging numbers to the bin count. The annotated copy is training material; any operative outcome must be found in its governing original, not inferred from this example.\n\n- Exercise 6: A teaching table deliberately included an unclosed column. Readers were asked to locate a certified closure instead of inferring that no late movement had occurred. The annotated copy is training material; any operative outcome must be found in its governing original, not inferred from this example.\n\n---\nSigned operative block\n\nSteward movement slip, Juniper Crate, 2026-10-12. Newly quarantined: 8; broken: 2. Neither group was already excluded from the October opening usable count. Both are removed from usable stock. A draft request for 10 filters is unposted and changes no count. This complete movement slip closes the October ledger through 2026-10-13."
      },
