ning was real evidence of that warning, not evidence that no failures occurred elsewhere.\n\nThe station file was retained as a reference exercise. Its facilitator could recommend clearer filing, but had no authority to alter Tidal Canary's signed policy or make a binding decision for the requested case.\n\n### Workshop station 6\nFuture monitoring software changed endpoint conventions. The operations board's dated policy, rather than deployment chatter, determined which endpoint convention governed the evaluation.\n\nThe station file was retained as a reference exercise. Its facilitator could recommend clearer filing, but had no authority to alter Tidal Canary's signed policy or make a binding decision for the requested case.\n\n---\nSigned operative block\n\nMonitor desk complete canary failure extract for Tidal Canary, evaluation 2026-10-13T10:30:00Z. Closed window: 10:00:00Z through 10:30:00Z. Failures in that window: 7, including one exactly at 10:00. An additional failure at 09:59:59 and two warnings are excluded. No unlisted failures occur in this window. This is the signed complete extract.\n\nSOURCE {\"aliases\":[\"Tidal Canary\",\"Tidal Canary rollback\",\"Tidal Canary monitor\"],\"authored_at\":\"2026-08-24T08:00:00Z\",\"chars\":[0,337],\"id\":\"N088-R013\",\"incorporates\":[],\"kind\":\"source\",\"links\":[\"N088-R006\"],\"revision\":2,\"scope\":\"N088\",\"supersedes\":[\"N088-R012\"],\"title\":\"Tidal Canary operative amendment\"}\nOperations board recovery rule for Tidal Canary, effective 2026-09-01. For the canary lane, roll back when failure count is strictly greater than 6 in the closed trailing 30-minute window. Count events at both endpoints, discard earlier events, and do not count warnings. A complete signed event extract is delegated to the monitor desk.\n\nSOURCE {\"aliases\":[\"Cedar Canary\",\"Cedar Canary rollback\",\"Cedar Canary monitor\"],\"authored_at\":\"2026-08-24T08:00:00Z\",\"chars\":[0,337],\"id\":\"N085-R008\",\"incorporates\":[],